      <memberdef kind="function" id="journal_8h_1ace69f4e2d55588ec12e467f0f88cee5f" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void journal_set</definition>
        <argsstring>(struct journal *new_journal)</argsstring>
        <name>journal_set</name>
        <param>
          <type>struct <ref refid="structjournal" kindref="compound">journal</ref> *</type>
          <declname>new_journal</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Change the current implementation of the journaling API. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Happens during life cycle of an instance:</para><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>When recovering a snapshot, the log sequence numbers don&apos;t matter and are not used, transactions can be recovered in any order. A stub API simply returns 0 for every write request.</para></listitem><listitem><para>When recovering from the local write ahead log, the LSN of each entry is already known. In this case, the journal API should simply return the existing log sequence numbers of records and do nothing else.</para></listitem></orderedlist>
<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>After recovery, in wal_mode = NONE, the implementation fakes a WAL by using a simple counter to provide log sequence numbers.</para></listitem><listitem><para>If the write ahead log is on, the WAL thread is issuing the log sequence numbers. </para></listitem></orderedlist>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/tsafin/tarantool/src/box/journal.h" line="187" column="1" bodyfile="/home/tsafin/tarantool/src/box/journal.h" bodystart="187" bodyend="190"/>
      </memberdef>
